    "id": "pqueue-4872154a",
    "title": "Replace in-memory secondary indexes with axon-esf typed keys",
    "description": "Replace ADR-010 raw length-prefixed byte index key encoding in crates/pqueue-projection with axon_esf typed index key helpers from axon-esf v0.3.2 for typed queues, while preserving legacy IndexSpec raw-byte behavior. Prior repairs closed update_fields None preservation, typed string lookup ambiguity, legacy raw-byte exactness, and objectlog/in-memory projection constructors, but focused review found remaining blockers: sqlite/postgres log-replay projection construction still omits .with_typed_indexes; fresh upsert insert paths in memory/sqlite/postgres call legacy-only index_validate without entity, and sqlite/postgres update_fields validate with legacy-only index_validate_update, allowing typed unique conflicts to commit. Fix these before advancing. In-scope files: pqueue-memory, pqueue-sqlite, pqueue-postgres, pqueue-projection tests or facade/backend tests as needed. Out-of-scope: relational SQL typed index tables and public typed query API beyond preserving current safe projection behavior.",
    "acceptance": "cargo fmt --check passes; cargo test -p pqueue secondary_indexes -- --nocapture passes; cargo test -p pqueue-projection --lib -- --nocapture passes; tests cover typed unique conflict rejection for upsert insert and update_fields on memory plus sqlite log-replay where available without env; sqlite/postgres log-replay ProjectionData constructors and rebuild/open paths call .with_typed_indexes(\u0026definition.typed_indexes); memory/sqlite/postgres upsert insert validation passes replacement entity_document into typed-aware unique validation; sqlite/postgres update_fields validation passes set_entity_document into typed-aware update validation; rg -n 'ProjectionData::new|index_validate\\(|index_validate_update\\(' crates/pqueue-memory/src/lib.rs crates/pqueue-sqlite/src/lib.rs crates/pqueue-postgres/src/lib.rs shows no remaining typed-index-capable path using legacy-only validation where entity_document is available.",
    "parent": "pqueue-fc8ef1aa",
